{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: c9133b2f448115c7434414aa18a44dda94bc5f87 on request/url-observation-host-binding, two commits over main e3ad5f92, four changed paths, live exact-path artifacts at that head named (normaliser 2b2aa9b8 is the lane's newest report and cites requester finding 35bd5de8), checkout clean, commits rest on request #4086. This replaces my approval #4096 of the superseded head f4f9ef0c.\n\nDelta from f4f9ef0c: the userinfo class gains the literal asterisk (\\x2a), two regression cases for u*ser and u%2Aser, an output-limit test, and paragraphs in the README and Stage 1 note that state the separate 256 KiB output-limit evaluation error and projection gap for a near-cap valid observation, with no truncation.\n\nReproduced at the head: all eleven CI gates green (root and jsonataddl test, race and vet; boundary; root module; both vulnerability scans; demo; clean checkout). Mutation control: with the f4f9ef0c normaliser overlaid, TestURLReputationNormalizerActualAuthorityHost/userinfo-literal-asterisk fails; exact bytes restored. Grammar probe: one positive input per RFC 3986 userinfo symbol (every unreserved and sub-delim character, the colon, and both cases of the percent-encoded asterisk), 22 of 22 accepted with the URL stored exactly. Controls retained: the asterisk variant of the colon spoof (example.com*:pw@evil.test with host example.com), the colon and numeric-port spoofs, double at-sign and whitespace in the authority all refuse; bracketed IPv6 with a port accepts; the new output-limit test confirms a near-cap valid observation returns the evaluation error while the same-size wrong host is ineffective and eventless.\n\nArchitecture: bundle fold, its test and two documents; runtime, schema, tables, exports and evaluator capabilities unchanged; the bounded 18-step first-at-sign search is unchanged from the previously reviewed head and remains the smallest construction available within the allow-list. Security: actual-host binding after valid userinfo, spoof and malformed-authority refusals and exact URL retention all hold with the wider class; the asterisk adds no delimiter the parser relies on. Simplification: one character in a class plus tests and honest documentation; nothing to cut.\n\nThe lowercase-versus-IDNA limitation is not claimed fixed and belongs to #4087, as the request states.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:45112fdc1a7ee699105986d83674222b2aa9b8f3","head":"c9133b2f448115c7434414aa18a44dda94bc5f87","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:45112fdc1a7ee699105986d83674222b2aa9b8f3\",\"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:d6df084823157d5594d7916ee7c37d9b8621bc42\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:d6df084823157d5594d7916ee7c37d9b8621bc42","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:1683f1aacee8fe8a14ae3d6a9efab9a371fe8f0a, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:353060694b1c4bda9a2ab15bfa05ac567e521fc9, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:37ffe552440312066313300b9e99b1aed510b2c7, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:45112fdc1a7ee699105986d83674222b2aa9b8f3, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:75e52432f5cec8fcca20528a1cd0bd7439fba479, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:d6df084823157d5594d7916ee7c37d9b8621bc42, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:fd9a80d440defc74e0733da3976af5bec196f52b stale; retired bases: git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:0a38cf2bea5866a24fc1eb6fdb211b4fac7e09a4, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:19b5ca6210ffdbf4ea29e419faae27649a60db46, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:1fb485d3c0f06ebac3bd50c0771285f773d283dd, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad